#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polylog

#% text
# `polylog(s, z)` gives the polylogarithm `Li_s(z)`, the sum of `z^k/k^s` for `k >= 1`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The series (DLMF 25.12.10) converges for `abs(z) < 1`; elsewhere the function is continued analytically, with a branch cut on `z > 1`.

#% item
# Exact values: `polylog(s, 0)` is 0, `polylog(s, 1)` is `zeta(s)` for `s > 1`, `polylog(1, z)` is `-log(1 - z)`, and integer `s <= 0` gives rational functions of `z`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `polylog` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polylog(2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.5822405264650125

#% cell
polylog(2, 1)
#% output
#= (1/6)*pi^2

#% cell
polylog(1, z)
#% output
#= -log(1 - z)

#% cell
polylog(3, -1.0)
#% output
#= -0.9015426773696957

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A negative integer order is a rational function:

#% cell
polylog(-1, z)
#% output
#= z/(1 - z)^2

#% text
# Outside the unit disc:

#% cell
polylog(2, -3.0)
#% output
#= -1.9393754207667089

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
polylog(2, 0.5*im)
#% output
#= -0.05897507442156586 + 0.4872223582945224im

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(polylog(2, 1/2), 30)
#% output
#= 0.582240526465012505902656320159680

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The series:

#% cell
sum(0.5^k/k^2, [k, 1, 60]) - polylog(2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 1.1102230246251565e-16

#% text
# The derivative in `z`:

#% cell
d(polylog(3, z), z)
#% output
#= polylog(2, z)/z

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `zeta`, `lerch_phi`, `log`
